/* Modern theme for the generic confirm dialog -- forged-dialog construction (base.rcss's
   .modern-shell-edge/.modern-groove/.modern-content-well/.modern-footer), the same primitives
   Login/SysMenu use, rather than the flatter .modern-frame/.modern-frame-accent pair this file
   used before. #panel's own background/border/box-shadow recipe matches sys_menu.rcss's #panel
   exactly (both are small forged-iron dialogs with no hero-banner). No header rail/title plate --
   this dialog has no title, unlike Login/SysMenu. */

/* #panel is centered via .center-both, not a GetProperty()-read-back calc -- same reasoning as
   remember_password_prompt.rcss. dp throughout: this is a LayoutMode::Dialog window (no
   transform:scale(root_scale)), not one of the root_scale-tracking inventory-family windows. */
#panel {
	width: 230dp;
	height: 160dp;
	font-family: "token(font-body)";
	font-size: 12dp;
	color: token(text-primary);
	border-radius: token(radius-sm)dp;
	background-color: #080a08;
	decorator: linear-gradient(to bottom, #11130f 0%, #080a08 100%);
	border-width: 1dp;
	border-color: token(border-frame);
	box-shadow:
		0 11dp 30dp rgba(0, 0, 0, 158),
		0 2dp 5dp rgba(0, 0, 0, 217),
		inset 0 0 0 1dp #090a08,
		inset 0 0 0 3dp rgba(120, 115, 90, 190);
}

/* Recessed message well -- base.rcss's .modern-content-well (shared with no other consumer yet)
   sized/positioned for this dialog's own panel. Text sits directly on the well, scrolling
   (overflow: auto hidden) rather than growing the panel -- see the top-level
   generic_confirm_dialog.rml's own comment for why (the Quest window's .quest-contents proves the
   same technique).

   top+bottom (not top+height) deliberately -- this element also has flex centering below, and this
   engine's box model is content-box only (no box-sizing support anywhere in this codebase); an
   explicit height combined with flex/padding on children pushed the box past its intended bottom
   edge and visually overlapped the button row. Anchoring both edges keeps the box's outer size
   exactly (right - left) x (bottom - top) regardless of its content's own layout. Content centers
   via flex (column direction, both axes), matching the reference's `place-items:center` -- the
   message reads centered whether it's one short line or several. */
.gcd-body {
	position: absolute;
	left: 16dp;
	right: 16dp;
	top: 10dp;
	bottom: 54dp;
	overflow: auto hidden;
	display: flex;
	flex-direction: column;
	justify-content: center;
	align-items: center;
}
.gcd-line {
	display: block;
	width: 100%;
	text-align: center;
	white-space: normal;
	color: token(text-secondary);
	font-effect: shadow(0dp 1dp #000000);
}
.gcd-line.bold { font-weight: bold; color: token(text-warm); }

/* Divider between the message well and the button row -- base.rcss's .modern-footer, repositioned
   to sit just above the buttons instead of flush with the panel's bottom edge. */
.gcd-footer {
	left: 8dp;
	right: 8dp;
	top: 114dp;
	bottom: auto;
}

.btn.gcd-btn-primary, .btn.gcd-btn-secondary {
	top: 120dp;
	width: 60dp;
	height: 25dp;
	line-height: 25dp;
}
.gcd-btn-primary   { left: 32dp; }
.gcd-btn-primary.solo { left: 85dp; }
.gcd-btn-secondary { left: 138dp; }
